From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: apple: stop the USB controller and port controllers for
 a deep sleep

A deep sleep powers off the controller's domain, and the sleep engine
needs ATC0_COMMON off, so keeping the core up as a syscore device can't
work: the suspend is refused, and it would find a dead core if it
weren't. xHCI can't resume across that either.

dwc3-apple already knows how to stop everything and start again, for a
cable disconnect. Do the same around a deep sleep: stop before the
freezer runs and start once the system is back, when firmware for what's
behind the hub can be found. USB devices come back as new devices, so a
mounted USB disk doesn't survive this. The wakeup setting is turned off
for the sleep, as it would keep the domain on, and a role that arrives
during the sleep is applied afterwards. A controller is always stopped.

macOS sends the port controllers SSPS with state 3 before a sleep. tipd
does that where the tree asks for it with apple,sleep-ssps, and goes
back to S0 after. A controller that doesn't take it only logs.

The sleep controller ends the debug link with a cold reset of its port
controller, which leaves that firmware's interrupt mask and power state
at their defaults. tipd sets the controller up again when the link was
cut, and rearms the link where the tree gives the board's key in
apple,debug-lock-key, as a boot loader does: unlock, debug mode on,
enable the debug VDM, debug mode off, lock. A failure only logs.

The ATC PHY forgets what its DisplayPort side owned or was stopping once
its domain has been off, since none of that survives.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>

[j604 backport: context conflicts only. dwc3-apple.c: this tree's glue has no T8132 tunables, drd_cfg or host_only, so only <linux/suspend.h>, pm_nb and the three sleep fields are added; selftest mocks.c: the sleep fields added to this tree's struct. Uses apple_sleep_debug_link_was_cut()/_cut_peek(), stubs in sleep.h (apple-s2r cuts no debug link). On J604 the tipd half is inert (no apple,sleep-ssps or apple,debug-lock-key in the DT); the glue stops and restarts the three controllers whenever "mem" is deep.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
